Subject: [PATCH] Vectorize independent small-model outputs without reordering sums (#1116)

The hidden layers have 750 outputs stored contiguously in each weight row.
Visit a whole row at a time instead of walking the matrix at a 3000-byte
stride. Each output still accumulates inputs from left to right and adds
its bias last; there is no horizontal SIMD reduction or fast-math flag.
Keep the three-output final layer's existing computation unchanged.
Limit the new path to Apple builds; Linux retains its qualified computation.

diff --git a/deepvariant/native/small_model_inference.mm b/deepvariant/native/small_model_inference.mm
--- a/deepvariant/native/small_model_inference.mm
+++ b/deepvariant/native/small_model_inference.mm
@@ -20,5 +20,5 @@
-// Inference is strict-scalar sequential FP32: per output element a
-// scalar `for` accumulator, no SIMD reduction, no `mad`/FMA — same
-// pattern as `bnns_finalize.mm`. This produces output identical to
-// Eigen+single-thread on x86 within 1 ULP and matches Docker's
-// dispatch decisions on the chr20 cross-MID sites.
+// Inference keeps left-to-right FP32 accumulation for each output.
+// On Apple, the hidden layers vectorize across independent outputs,
+// not across the input reduction. No fast-math flags are enabled.
+// Keep the final three-output layer's original computation: its
+// rounding determines small-model dispatch near GQ thresholds.
@@ -96,6 +96,21 @@
 void DenseFp32(const float* x, int in_dim,
                const float* W, const float* b,
                int out_dim, float* y) {
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+  if (out_dim >= 4) {
+    // Independent outputs are SIMD lanes, never a horizontal reduction.
+    // Each output still accumulates inputs in order and adds its bias last.
+    std::fill(y, y + out_dim, 0.0f);
+    for (int i = 0; i < in_dim; ++i) {
+      const float* row = W + i * out_dim;
+      for (int o = 0; o < out_dim; ++o) {
+        y[o] += x[i] * row[o];
+      }
+    }
+    for (int o = 0; o < out_dim; ++o) y[o] += b[o];
+    return;
+  }
+#endif
